@using ProgrammePulse.Models.SkillsEvidence

@*
    The rubric, shown wherever someone has to pick a level. Repeating the
    words next to the choice is deliberate: the levels only mean anything
    if the person choosing and the person reviewing read the same
    description at the moment they decide.
*@
<details class="ops-panel">
    <summary><strong>What the proficiency levels mean</strong></summary>
    <dl>
        @foreach (var level in ProficiencyRubric.All)
        {
            <dt><strong>@level</strong></dt>
            <dd>@ProficiencyRubric.Describe(level)</dd>
        }
    </dl>
    <p class="ops-empty-state">
        A level is set by a person and reviewed by a person. Nothing in this system
        infers a level from activity — not commits, not tickets, not hours logged.
        Validated levels fall due for review after @ProficiencyRubric.DefaultReviewIntervalMonths months.
    </p>
</details>
